WEBVTT

00:02.690 --> 00:04.040
You're an idiot.

00:04.480 --> 00:07.380
It's bad enough you believed her, but then you gave up?

00:07.810 --> 00:09.560
Please, forgive me Colonel.

00:09.880 --> 00:11.110
You've gotta stay strong.

00:11.380 --> 00:13.560
And don't you ever give up on living.

00:13.930 --> 00:17.000
I need to know you can keep
your cool no matter what happens.

00:18.070 --> 00:18.880
Sir.

00:20.110 --> 00:22.810
I'm gonna continue to
rely on you to watch my back.

00:23.020 --> 00:24.100
Don't let me down.

00:24.340 --> 00:27.200
You oughta think about taking
your own advice, Colonel.

00:27.430 --> 00:29.760
Since you were the one
who abandoned his post.

00:29.780 --> 00:31.750
Hey! Shut up, Havoc—ow!

00:31.750 --> 00:33.000
[GROANS]

00:33.670 --> 00:34.780
And what the hell?

00:34.990 --> 00:36.840
Why are we even in the same room?

00:37.080 --> 00:39.040
At my rank I should have my own room.

00:39.100 --> 00:40.060
With hot nurse...

00:40.400 --> 00:41.780
Try to understand, sir.

00:42.310 --> 00:44.820
It's easier to guard the
two of you in the same place.

00:44.890 --> 00:46.260
Which reminds me...

00:46.930 --> 00:49.520
Why haven't they tried to kill us yet?

00:50.100 --> 00:51.660
What's wrong with you?!

00:51.760 --> 00:54.640
How could you let that bastard go
after what he did?

00:54.680 --> 00:57.060
You should've yanked his spine
out of his mouth!

00:57.840 --> 01:00.560
Lust... He killed Lust...

01:00.680 --> 01:03.860
It's not too late to kill him,
so get to it!

01:03.970 --> 01:05.660
We can use Mustang.

01:06.100 --> 01:08.240
He's worthless if we kill him, however.

01:08.500 --> 01:09.580
Use him?

01:09.880 --> 01:10.600
Hold on...

01:10.660 --> 01:12.060
You mean the portal?

01:12.260 --> 01:14.800
[CHUCKLES]
You don't need to worry about it

01:14.890 --> 01:16.240
And forget Mustang.

01:16.420 --> 01:18.860
Father wants me to handle him.

01:21.840 --> 01:27.560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

01:27.560 --> 01:32.980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

01:39.540 --> 01:42.860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

01:42.860 --> 01:45.540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

01:45.540 --> 01:51.840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

01:51.840 --> 01:57.960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

01:57.960 --> 02:04.040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

02:04.180 --> 02:10.200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

02:10.340 --> 02:17.080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

02:17.260 --> 02:22.620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

02:22.840 --> 02:29.340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

02:29.340 --> 02:35.100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

02:35.100 --> 02:41.300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

02:41.300 --> 02:48.120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

02:48.120 --> 02:52.240

02:52.330 --> 02:54.260
What if I've started to rot?

02:54.260 --> 02:55.240
BOTH: Huh?

02:55.640 --> 02:59.600
I doubt that my body's getting any nutrients...
or any sleep, either!

02:59.860 --> 03:02.600
So even if we get it
back from over there...

03:02.660 --> 03:05.560
[DISTORTED] Brother... Winry...

03:05.560 --> 03:07.410
[SHRIEKS]

03:08.500 --> 03:10.000
Is he right, Ed?

03:10.760 --> 03:11.620
[SIGH]

03:11.740 --> 03:13.580
Now this is just a hypothesis...

03:13.720 --> 03:17.500
But I was thinking about the transmutation
and trying to retrace our process.

03:17.660 --> 03:21.580
You remember how we mixed our blood
to create a blueprint for mom's soul?

03:21.700 --> 03:22.660
Yeah.

03:22.740 --> 03:25.600
Well, right after that
we passed through the portal,

03:25.760 --> 03:27.560
where we were both deconstructed.

03:29.440 --> 03:30.580
It's a slim chance...

03:30.740 --> 03:34.820
But I think it's possible our spirits
might've gotten tangled up in the process.

03:35.800 --> 03:37.280
What are you saying?

03:37.330 --> 03:40.440
I'm trying to explain that our
bodies might be connected somehow,

03:40.460 --> 03:43.120
even though I'm
here and your body's over there.

03:43.260 --> 03:44.100
See...

03:44.110 --> 03:47.180
That might actually explain why I'm so sh...

03:48.560 --> 03:50.020
Sh...

03:50.860 --> 03:52.080
Short.

03:52.150 --> 03:55.280
- He admitted it.
- He's starting to face reality!

03:55.420 --> 03:56.240
So...

03:56.640 --> 04:00.340
You think you've been supplying
all the nutrients for Al's body, too?

04:00.740 --> 04:02.630
That seems a little far-fetched.

04:02.860 --> 04:04.820
Well what's your explanation?

04:05.020 --> 04:07.480
You don't grow because
you refuse to drink your milk.

04:07.640 --> 04:10.380
- Don't start with that again!
- Well, it's true!

04:10.400 --> 04:13.080
It seems like brother is always sleeping...

04:13.100 --> 04:16.400
I wonder if his body could
be resting for mine as well?

04:16.420 --> 04:18.360
...you start drinking it, you have to!

04:18.360 --> 04:19.460
- It's not gonna happen!
- Drink it!

04:19.460 --> 04:20.050
No!

04:20.050 --> 04:21.100
- Fine, stay a runt!
- [AL LAUGHING]

04:21.120 --> 04:22.060
I'm not a runt!

04:22.140 --> 04:23.160
I hope so, at least.

04:23.160 --> 04:25.960
- ...Never!
- I'll make you!
- Just try!

04:28.220 --> 04:29.880
Are you here to visit the Colonel?

04:29.900 --> 04:32.040
Mr. Havoc is recovering too.

04:32.290 --> 04:34.370
We figured we should pay our respects.

04:34.540 --> 04:36.340
I definitely owe it to the Colonel.

04:36.360 --> 04:38.440
He saved me right the last second.

04:40.060 --> 04:42.280
Are you also dropping by for a visit?

04:42.880 --> 04:44.560
And bringing a little present.

04:46.520 --> 04:50.720
I counted the number of steps it took to get
to the basement under the Third Laboratory.

04:50.900 --> 04:54.180
And I was able to calculate
the approximate location of that doorway.

04:55.260 --> 04:57.400
It's not exact, since the hallway curved

04:57.670 --> 05:01.370
But I was able to deduce a radius
with the lab at the center.

05:03.280 --> 05:04.920
That's Central Command?!

05:05.020 --> 05:07.120
But this is even more alarming...

05:07.500 --> 05:09.260
It's the Presidential Estate.

05:09.520 --> 05:11.960
Right above where we found
the homunculi.

05:12.460 --> 05:17.150
Which means there's a very real possibility
the Fuhrer is connected to them.

05:18.580 --> 05:19.930
But that doesn't make sense.

05:20.340 --> 05:23.940
Why did he kill Greed and his group
if he's connected to them?

05:24.220 --> 05:25.920
Strange he killed them anyway...

05:26.140 --> 05:29.020
Why would he slaughter them
before interrogating them?

05:29.820 --> 05:31.080
Strange, all right.

05:31.240 --> 05:32.960
Damn inscrutable.

05:34.740 --> 05:38.540
One thing's for sure, the enemy's infiltrated
high up the command.

05:38.620 --> 05:41.350
So extreme caution is
necessary at all times

05:41.660 --> 05:42.780
And Fullmetal?

05:43.060 --> 05:45.160
- Watch yourself.
- [GASP]

05:48.460 --> 05:51.260
The Fuhrer...working with the Homunculi...

05:53.620 --> 05:56.120
This could be bigger
than I ever dreamed.

05:56.400 --> 05:58.680
I'm starting to worry that it's too big.

05:59.020 --> 06:00.640
All the more reason to pursue it.

06:01.480 --> 06:01.900
So.

06:02.320 --> 06:04.340
I hope you're ready
to work yourselves ragged.

06:04.360 --> 06:06.530
Oh, yeah. About that, Colonel?

06:07.180 --> 06:09.040
I think you're gonna have to count me out.

06:11.900 --> 06:13.540
Your work requires legs

06:14.160 --> 06:16.160
- And I can't feel mine.
- [GASPS]

06:18.000 --> 06:19.880
I hate to say it,

06:19.960 --> 06:21.290
but I'm retired.

06:28.100 --> 06:29.270
Hello.

06:29.760 --> 06:30.720
Hey.

06:31.060 --> 06:32.460
What brings you down here?

06:32.720 --> 06:34.190
Back problems.

06:34.330 --> 06:38.150
My spine can't stand all the standing
that comes with being coroner.

06:41.200 --> 06:45.440
I got a sinking feeling when I heard
you were the person that scorched that Thing.

06:45.840 --> 06:47.690
Are you plotting something?

06:47.840 --> 06:51.640
You suspect a plot, but you still ID'd the "thing" as Maria Ross.

06:52.000 --> 06:54.060
Three cheers for old war buddies, huh?

06:54.220 --> 06:55.870
Old war buddies, my butt.

06:56.200 --> 06:57.680
More like accomplices.

06:58.360 --> 07:00.970
You'd incinerate 'em
and I'd dissect what's left.

07:01.450 --> 07:04.670
We treated them like rats
and Ishval was the lab.

07:09.220 --> 07:11.040
I know you like to play with fire,

07:11.040 --> 07:13.620
but someone'll get burnt
if you push this too far.

07:14.060 --> 07:15.700
You should have warned me earlier.

07:15.840 --> 07:16.380
Huh?

07:18.820 --> 07:20.690
Did somebody get injured?

07:22.140 --> 07:23.640
One of my men.

07:25.420 --> 07:26.740
He was paralyzed.

07:27.320 --> 07:28.700
From the waist down.

07:34.540 --> 07:35.480
Damn.

07:35.640 --> 07:39.260
They only let me smoke one of these a day,
and I go and waste it.

07:40.540 --> 07:41.540
Jeez.

07:41.590 --> 07:45.080
You know I thought I'd retire because
of a woman, but not like this.

07:46.120 --> 07:47.600
So what happens next?

07:49.180 --> 07:51.440
My family owns a grocery store.

07:52.420 --> 07:54.180
And I can at least take calls.

07:54.980 --> 07:56.980
Isn't automail an option?

07:59.220 --> 08:02.060
The nerves in my lower spine
are completely severed,

08:02.080 --> 08:04.430
and they can't make those out of steel.

08:04.640 --> 08:05.400
Tch.

08:06.000 --> 08:08.240
The retired life
doesn't suit you.

08:13.080 --> 08:13.940
Colonel.

08:13.940 --> 08:14.660
Hmm?

08:15.360 --> 08:16.920
There's still hope for Havoc.

08:17.380 --> 08:18.920
Fullmetal passed this onto me.

08:21.460 --> 08:22.910
Dr. Marcoh, huh?

08:23.660 --> 08:26.200
Medical alchemist in possession of a...

08:26.260 --> 08:28.220
Philosopher's stone?!

08:28.420 --> 08:30.420
Well, sir, should I find him?

08:31.750 --> 08:32.920
Permission granted.

08:33.040 --> 08:34.390
Get going.

08:38.900 --> 08:40.320
Oh, Major!

08:40.740 --> 08:41.340
Hmm?

08:41.380 --> 08:43.030
I didn't expect
you back so soon.

08:43.500 --> 08:45.620
How did you enjoy
your vacation to the east?

08:45.620 --> 08:47.620
[GRUNTING]

08:47.620 --> 08:48.250
Shh!

08:48.250 --> 08:50.480
Loose lips sink ships, Major.

08:51.040 --> 08:54.260
The scenery was luminous
and the women desirable.

08:54.300 --> 08:55.100
Ha...

08:55.540 --> 08:57.280
Uh, oh! Uh, before I forget,

08:57.400 --> 09:00.080
this just arrived from the Provost Marshal's office.

09:00.720 --> 09:03.540
It's an urgent bulletin
for all State Alchemists.

09:04.560 --> 09:06.020
Good heavens!

09:09.580 --> 09:10.700
How'd it go?

09:10.800 --> 09:11.420
Easy.

09:11.560 --> 09:15.670
I told them I was a State Alchemist and they
let me right in with no questions asked.

09:16.020 --> 09:17.690
Did you find the basement?

09:17.800 --> 09:18.760
There wasn't one.

09:18.760 --> 09:19.720
[GASP]

09:20.350 --> 09:23.450
But it did find a trace
of some hasty alchemy.

09:24.200 --> 09:27.890
It was stupid of us to think that
they wouldn't seal up the entrance.

09:29.020 --> 09:29.740
I guess so.

09:30.060 --> 09:33.400
Where else are we gonna to find a
homunculus if we can get down there?

09:34.870 --> 09:35.930
I'm not sure.

09:36.680 --> 09:40.060
Remember how they told me I was their sacrifice,
and they needed me alive?

09:40.140 --> 09:41.580
They told me the same thing.

09:41.860 --> 09:44.990
Lust told me that when
she found out I opened the portal.

09:45.060 --> 09:46.750
Well there's one piece of the puzzle.

09:46.940 --> 09:48.400
They're looking for alchemists...

09:48.400 --> 09:51.710
that managed to open the portal
and make it back out alive.

09:51.940 --> 09:54.860
But the real question is
why they wanna sacrifice us.

09:55.140 --> 09:57.700
So, we'll have to beat an answer out of them.

09:58.360 --> 10:00.000
- Edward, wait!
- What the...

10:00.220 --> 10:01.600
Is that Sergeant Brosh?

10:01.600 --> 10:02.860
I'm glad I found you.

10:03.020 --> 10:04.760
Yeah, why don't you tell me what's wrong?

10:04.760 --> 10:07.000
You should go back to your hotel right now.

10:07.440 --> 10:09.360
I can escort you if you want me to.

10:11.260 --> 10:13.360
Attention all military personnel,

10:13.610 --> 10:16.740
It has been verified that
Scar has returned to central.

10:16.860 --> 10:18.720
Three casualties have been reported.

10:19.100 --> 10:21.540
All confirmed as State Alchemists.

10:22.220 --> 10:23.840
According to eyewitness reports,

10:23.940 --> 10:28.040
he is described as an Ishvalan,
with an X-shaped scar on his forehead.

10:28.280 --> 10:31.920
Other identifiable markings include
a tattoo on his right arm.

10:34.320 --> 10:35.560
A tattoo.

10:36.440 --> 10:37.890
It was him.

10:38.640 --> 10:40.470
Fullmetal Alchemist

10:42.120 --> 10:43.740
Fullmetal Alchemist.

10:44.960 --> 10:48.130
So you're saying that
Scar killed Winry's parents?

10:48.360 --> 10:50.820
I don't know for certain,
but that's the way it looks.

10:51.160 --> 10:52.470
Poor Winry...

10:52.760 --> 10:53.520
Brother,

10:53.540 --> 10:55.560
you weren't planning on
telling her, were you?

10:55.700 --> 10:56.780
Of course not, Al.

10:57.540 --> 11:00.320
I couldn't stand to be the one
to make her cry again.

11:01.420 --> 11:02.800
Neither could i.

11:04.490 --> 11:07.430
It's the last thing I wanna do,
but we have to confront Scar

11:07.790 --> 11:09.080
To find out if he did it?

11:09.520 --> 11:11.030
Well, that's one reason.

11:11.240 --> 11:12.900
But there is another.

11:13.060 --> 11:15.100
We're gonna lure out the Homunculi.

11:15.520 --> 11:16.280
[GASP]

11:16.280 --> 11:19.100
They need us alive
for their sacrifice, don't they?

11:19.400 --> 11:23.030
So I doubt they'll be willing to just
stand by while Scar kills us.

11:23.750 --> 11:24.590
You think so?

11:25.100 --> 11:27.320
Sounds like a pretty
big gamble to me.

11:27.710 --> 11:29.570
Well it's much better
than doin' nothing.

11:29.990 --> 11:30.680
Oh, really?

11:30.860 --> 11:33.420
Because Scar literally torn us apart
the last time.

11:34.610 --> 11:36.880
Well, we've...gotten stronger...

11:36.880 --> 11:38.540
in these past few months...

11:39.060 --> 11:41.390
What happens if the Homunculi do show up?

11:41.640 --> 11:43.120
How are you gonna catch one?!

11:43.190 --> 11:46.400
They're super strong,
and they pretty much can't die!

11:46.520 --> 11:48.960
Can't die? Was that hyperbole?

11:49.080 --> 11:50.900
Or are they actually immortal?

11:52.500 --> 11:54.400
Why don't we lock the windows?

11:55.820 --> 11:58.560
Count us in,
we'd love to help you guys.

11:58.560 --> 11:59.420
Why's that?

11:59.540 --> 12:02.080
I can't say I care about the military stuff,

12:02.080 --> 12:05.500
but it sounds like these Homunculi are
just what we've been looking for.

12:07.860 --> 12:08.720
What's wrong?

12:08.780 --> 12:10.440
You look kindaskeptical.

12:10.840 --> 12:14.180
Don't get me wrong, I am grateful for
the help you've already given...

12:14.180 --> 12:16.800
- But this...
- You've got better odds with more help.

12:18.080 --> 12:19.490
I'm serious about this.

12:19.960 --> 12:22.530
This could be what
rescues my clan.

12:28.240 --> 12:29.740
Alright then.

12:30.350 --> 12:32.800
Just remember, we're in this together.

12:33.080 --> 12:34.980
I promise not to
run off with them.

12:35.460 --> 12:37.040
I owe you that much.

12:37.300 --> 12:38.320
What for?

12:40.500 --> 12:41.820
[CASH REGISTER DING]

12:41.900 --> 12:44.140
- Is...this...for room service?!

12:44.140 --> 12:45.640
Uhh... [NERVOUS LAUGH]

12:46.080 --> 12:48.020
You're damn right you owe me!

12:48.020 --> 12:49.260
[WINDOW SMASHES]
BOTH: Woo!

12:49.300 --> 12:50.980
Will you guys shut up?!

12:50.980 --> 12:53.320
Do you know how early
I have to wake up tomorrow?!

12:53.420 --> 12:55.140
Oh right, I forgot!

12:55.180 --> 12:57.520
You're catching an early train to Rush Va—

12:57.520 --> 13:00.180
[GASP]
[METAL SMASHING]

13:00.280 --> 13:02.300
Y'know what? You should cancel that.

13:02.440 --> 13:04.180
Why don't you stick around and relax?

13:04.200 --> 13:05.000
Huh?

13:05.440 --> 13:07.660
I mean it's just that...y'know, well...

13:07.740 --> 13:08.460
There's...

13:08.520 --> 13:10.960
Always a chance my arm could get broken.

13:11.340 --> 13:12.110
Or even...

13:12.180 --> 13:12.920
destroyed...

13:12.940 --> 13:15.380
[CRASH]
Are you planning on destroying it?!

13:15.560 --> 13:18.380
ED: [WHIMPERING]
AL: I've got your soul, brother!

13:19.280 --> 13:20.580
I can't believe you.

13:21.500 --> 13:24.360
Just promise you won't
do anything too dangerous.

13:25.230 --> 13:26.230
BOTH: Uh...

13:28.960 --> 13:32.180
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

13:32.300 --> 13:33.260
[KNOCKING]
Hey, Doc.

13:33.440 --> 13:34.640
Are you home?

13:34.920 --> 13:36.700
I could use your help with something.

13:38.810 --> 13:39.810
Huh?

13:45.460 --> 13:46.520
Damn.

13:49.700 --> 13:51.150
Is that so?

13:51.280 --> 13:53.220
Report back to base.

13:54.800 --> 13:56.580
Yet another dead end.

13:58.860 --> 14:01.260
[DOOR OPENS]

14:03.350 --> 14:06.060
Well, if you'll excuse me.

14:10.550 --> 14:11.270
Who was that?

14:11.720 --> 14:14.820
My mother, and an officer
from the veterans council.

14:16.000 --> 14:18.380
I've decided to go
ahead with my retirement.

14:19.600 --> 14:22.590
I don't know for certain if
your wounds are inoperable.

14:22.920 --> 14:25.220
I'm not dumb enough
to think i have a chance.

14:25.670 --> 14:26.790
I'm useless.

14:27.320 --> 14:28.380
You're wrong.

14:29.120 --> 14:32.240
Look, don't try and tell me
you need upon that can't move.

14:36.140 --> 14:38.400
And don't you
look at me like that.

14:39.110 --> 14:40.310
Forget about me.

14:40.790 --> 14:42.360
Move on already.

14:42.420 --> 14:44.480
You don't have time
to worry about me!

14:44.760 --> 14:47.480
You need to think about the promise
you made General Hughes,

14:47.520 --> 14:49.250
- instead of pitying me!
- Lieutenant Havoc!

14:55.720 --> 14:57.820
Just let me get on with my life.

14:59.600 --> 15:00.940
I beg you.

15:07.840 --> 15:09.150
- All right.
- [GASP]

15:09.440 --> 15:10.620
You're cut loose.

15:16.000 --> 15:18.440
I'll leave you behind
so you can catch up.

15:19.720 --> 15:21.020
I've got to keep moving,

15:21.290 --> 15:23.400
but I'll see you at the top.

15:25.820 --> 15:27.080
[DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES]

15:27.560 --> 15:28.980
He doesn't give up.

15:29.360 --> 15:31.960
He didn't even think about
turning his back on me.

15:31.960 --> 15:33.780
And I had given up on living.

15:34.300 --> 15:36.380
It's not in him to
abandon others.

15:36.640 --> 15:37.720
He refuses to.

15:40.010 --> 15:41.430
He's a fool.

15:41.540 --> 15:43.220
He's not gonna make it to the top.

15:43.520 --> 15:47.150
This country will chew him up
if he keeps on acting this soft.

15:48.100 --> 15:49.540
Well I don't know about that.

15:49.720 --> 15:52.280
This country needs
a fool like that man.

15:58.720 --> 16:01.000
I need you to bring me my uniform.

16:01.240 --> 16:03.720
But you're not ready to leave the hospital yet, Colonel.

16:03.760 --> 16:05.340
Just go get it.

16:10.500 --> 16:11.880
Right away, sir.

16:14.510 --> 16:17.620
Oh that's my livelihood, you idiot!

16:17.720 --> 16:19.640
U-Uh, I'm really sorry sir.

16:19.960 --> 16:23.040
Ah, well sorry's not gonna fix my stand.

16:23.480 --> 16:25.600
Looks like you could use some help!

16:25.600 --> 16:26.160
BOTH: Huh?

16:26.720 --> 16:28.580
It's a good thing I happened by!

16:28.580 --> 16:31.280
Edward Elric: State Alchemist at large!

16:35.020 --> 16:36.620
Wow, that's amazing!

16:36.820 --> 16:38.280
Thank you very much, sir!

16:38.280 --> 16:40.500
Please, you have to let me pay you for this.

16:40.760 --> 16:41.760
Pay me?

16:41.810 --> 16:44.060
Thats not necessary,
but thank you!

16:44.270 --> 16:46.980
Could you please help me
with my broken vase?

16:47.020 --> 16:49.080
It's a priceless family heirloom.

16:49.080 --> 16:51.080
Why no problem at all! [CLAP]

16:52.060 --> 16:53.360
[CROWD OOH'S]

16:54.220 --> 16:55.320
[CROWD OOH'S]

16:56.600 --> 16:58.100
[CROWD AHH'S]

17:00.860 --> 17:05.060
That's right, I'm here to help!
I'm your friendly neighborhood State Alchemist.

17:05.300 --> 17:07.780
Don't forget: I'm Edward Elric!

17:07.780 --> 17:09.780
[CROWD CHEERING]

17:10.520 --> 17:11.780
[SNEEZE]

17:12.680 --> 17:17.250
[CHUCKLING] I'm pretty sure everyone in
Central knows my name by now.

17:17.330 --> 17:19.360
Well you were a little over the top.

17:21.530 --> 17:24.860
When did you become so theatrical, Fullmetal?

17:25.120 --> 17:25.980
Colonel?

17:26.420 --> 17:28.440
Shouldn't you still
be in the hospital?

17:28.580 --> 17:29.580
Probably.

17:31.040 --> 17:32.810
I heard about Lieutenant Havoc.

17:33.290 --> 17:35.660
- I'm sure Doctor Marcoh—
- Hold on.

17:36.350 --> 17:37.940
People are watching us.

17:38.180 --> 17:39.360
Get in.

17:41.180 --> 17:43.380
On second thought let's get out.

17:45.020 --> 17:46.370
Dr. Marcoh's gone missing?

17:46.910 --> 17:47.660
Looks like it.

17:47.900 --> 17:49.920
They probably took him captive.

17:51.320 --> 17:53.150
There's something else
we need to talk about.

17:53.570 --> 17:55.460
I'm sure you've heard that Scar's back.

17:55.970 --> 17:59.610
So what's with the showboating,
do you want him to find you?

18:00.740 --> 18:02.480
Yeah that's exactly what I want.

18:03.110 --> 18:05.340
I need to fight him,
and you can't talk me out of it.

18:05.340 --> 18:07.100
Have you lost your mind?!

18:07.100 --> 18:10.410
Did you forget the way he
tore you apart in East City?

18:10.420 --> 18:13.600
Oooh, sounds like the Colonel's scared of big, bad Scar.

18:13.620 --> 18:17.560
I'm not surprised considering how useless
you were against him! [LAUGHING]

18:17.780 --> 18:20.200
That wasn't my fault,
it was raining that day!

18:20.220 --> 18:23.460
Was it raining when you got
beat up and sent to the hospital?

18:23.500 --> 18:25.600
You're still useless!

18:25.600 --> 18:26.920
Shut you mouth, Fullmetal!

18:30.200 --> 18:31.520
Guess he got your invite.

18:31.790 --> 18:32.600
You okay?

18:32.810 --> 18:35.910
He'd think it was raining
the way your forehead's dripping.

18:36.220 --> 18:37.070
Hold it!

18:37.460 --> 18:38.450
Don't shoot, Lieutenant.

18:38.780 --> 18:40.500
What? You can't be serious?!

18:40.560 --> 18:42.470
I'm trying out
the Colonel's sport.

18:42.620 --> 18:44.310
Think I might be able to catch a few fish.

18:50.680 --> 18:54.020
We're using brother as bait
to lure out the Homunculi

18:54.080 --> 18:55.430
He's too important to them.

18:55.680 --> 18:57.800
They can't afford to just let him die.

18:58.240 --> 18:59.420
That's crazy!

18:59.480 --> 19:01.640
We're not gonna let
anyone else get hurt.

19:01.790 --> 19:04.740
Using ourselves as bait
was our only option.

19:05.820 --> 19:08.340
What are you going to do
if Scar happens to get shot?

19:08.500 --> 19:10.880
The MPs might get here before the Homunculi.

19:10.920 --> 19:13.700
But you can stop that from happening.
Can't you, Colonel?

19:14.150 --> 19:16.190
So now I take orders
from you, is that it?

19:16.540 --> 19:18.060
You've got a lot of nerve.

19:19.020 --> 19:21.180
You had better plan on
sharing what you catch.

19:21.180 --> 19:22.240
Of course!

19:43.480 --> 19:46.060
Hey, get out of the way!
We need a clear shot.

19:46.060 --> 19:48.520
Don't shoot! You'll hit my brother!

19:48.940 --> 19:50.160
Dammit!

19:50.160 --> 19:52.580
Everything's lost if
those guys shoot Scar.

19:52.740 --> 19:54.320
How long can I keep this up?

19:54.500 --> 19:55.760
Way too close!

19:55.760 --> 19:57.760
Hurry up, you stupid Homunculi!

19:58.840 --> 20:01.380
Which channel's
the Provost Marshal's?

20:01.550 --> 20:02.030
Got it.

20:02.570 --> 20:04.650
You haven't let me down, Fuery..

20:06.020 --> 20:08.600
Attention, this is Sector 3 patrol.

20:08.600 --> 20:11.640
We're under attack from Scar,
request immediate backup—

20:11.800 --> 20:15.040
What? No! No—[SCREAMS]

20:15.040 --> 20:17.100
All right, onto Sector 17.

20:17.100 --> 20:19.200
[GIGGLING]
This is pretty fun!

20:19.420 --> 20:20.700
[LOW VOICE] Come in!
[DIFFERENT VOICE] Come in!

20:21.500 --> 20:22.860
But that can't be right...

20:22.960 --> 20:25.530
He's in Sector 17?
What about Sector 3?!

20:25.880 --> 20:26.920
Colonel Douglas!

20:27.100 --> 20:29.200
He's in Sector 8, now!
What's that?!

20:30.180 --> 20:32.380
MP HQ calling Sector 8.

20:32.680 --> 20:34.810
Scar is currently
fighting a young man.

20:34.930 --> 20:36.850
The young man is
a State Alchemist.

20:37.090 --> 20:38.330
Do not fire!

20:38.780 --> 20:40.260
Multiple reports in all sectors!

20:40.270 --> 20:41.840
We have reports of a fourth Scar!

20:41.920 --> 20:44.100
This is Sector 3,
all streets are clear.

20:44.300 --> 20:47.860
Sector 8 requesting backup!
Currently engaged with Scar!

20:53.040 --> 20:54.560
Come now, Gluttony.

20:54.560 --> 20:56.360
I smell the Ishvalan.

20:56.440 --> 20:58.360
He's here,
I get to eat him, right?!

21:00.280 --> 21:01.880
That's a strange presence.

21:01.880 --> 21:03.560
You could feel it too, right?

21:03.560 --> 21:04.660
Yes.

21:04.660 --> 21:06.140
Then it's time to move.

21:09.800 --> 21:11.220
Which will it be?

21:11.240 --> 21:13.540
Is he gonna destroy
my body or my automail?

21:13.540 --> 21:14.620
Brother!

21:21.720 --> 21:22.960
Lucky!

21:24.010 --> 21:26.270
He cancelled out Scar's alchemy!

21:26.470 --> 21:28.330
How reckless can you get?!

21:29.520 --> 21:31.430
He's got tattoo!

21:31.980 --> 21:33.080
Bastard!

21:33.610 --> 21:35.240
You were the one!

21:35.400 --> 21:38.140
I smell him!
Time to eat!

21:43.820 --> 21:45.800
Hi! How's it going?

21:46.180 --> 21:48.490
That is one pretty unusual
body you've got there.

21:49.210 --> 21:51.740
Just how many people
are inside you?

21:52.240 --> 21:53.810
Oh, you!

21:54.070 --> 21:55.700
Don't bother running.

21:55.870 --> 21:57.490
I sense your presence.

21:57.820 --> 21:59.420
And I can follow it.

21:59.840 --> 22:00.680
Follow? Me?

22:00.790 --> 22:01.790
Me?

22:02.660 --> 22:05.280
Then I'll just eat you now!

22:05.680 --> 22:06.310
There it is!

22:06.440 --> 22:07.960
He's a Homunculus!

22:08.410 --> 22:08.920
So,

22:09.350 --> 22:12.020
you're able to detect
his presence, are you?

22:14.620 --> 22:16.730
Well that's quite the nuisance.

22:17.540 --> 22:18.920
Let's take care of it.

22:20.800 --> 22:22.460
Lan Fan! Run!

22:25.640 --> 22:27.200
No! Lan Fan!

22:28.860 --> 22:34.400
Let it all out, let it all out

22:34.400 --> 22:38.760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

22:39.760 --> 22:45.100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

22:45.100 --> 22:51.120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

22:51.580 --> 22:56.820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

22:56.820 --> 23:02.200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

23:02.720 --> 23:11.960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

23:12.160 --> 23:17.580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

23:17.660 --> 23:23.840
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

23:23.840 --> 23:31.780
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

23:31.780 --> 23:34.040
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

23:34.040 --> 23:39.340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

23:39.340 --> 23:45.560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

23:45.560 --> 23:53.200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

23:53.440 --> 23:57.740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

24:00.140 --> 24:04.280
The scream of the fallen girl pierces
every darkened corner of Central.

24:04.960 --> 24:08.620
As the anguished debts of a violent history
are repaid with bloodshed,

24:08.720 --> 24:13.180
the past and present reveal themselves
to be murderous reflections of one another.

24:14.120 --> 24:16.790
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:17.500 --> 24:21.480
Episode 22: Backs in the Distance

24:22.100 --> 24:26.840
The young man realized... He'd do anything to protect her.
